{
  "contract": "native-schema-slices.md revision 5",
  "slice": "2h-root",
  "setup": {
    "notes": [
      "Attribute sizes are passed explicitly, as libbpf does (offsetofend of the last field used), so they do not depend on the probe's header version",
      "Runs as root with --root-bpf in the disposable probe VM, after the UID 1000 probe; every map and program is closed before NATIVE PASS",
      "array map: key 4, value 8, max_entries 4, name 'ant_array'; element 1 is set to 'ANTIMAP1' with BPF_ANY; deleting from an array is EINVAL",
      "map_lookup_batch starts with a NULL in_batch and count 4 over the whole array",
      "per-CPU array: key 4, value 8, max_entries 1; with 4 possible CPUs the value is 32 bytes",
      "prog_load: socket filter r0 = 0; exit, license 'GPL', log_level 1 with a 4096-byte log; prog_load_rejected: a lone exit, rejected by the verifier because R0 is not set",
      "prog_test_run runs the socket filter on a 64-byte zeroed frame with a 128-byte data_out",
      "obj_get_info_map asks for 64 bytes of bpf_map_info for the array map",
      "obj_get_missing names /sys/fs/bpf/ant-missing; raw_tracepoint_bad_prog attaches the socket filter to 'sched_switch'",
      "btf_load passes a 45-byte BTF blob: header, one 32-bit INT type named 'int', and its string table",
      "Attribute sizes from the pinned 6.12 header (sizeof(union bpf_attr) is 152): map_create 72, element ops 32, batch 56, prog_load with log 40, test_run 32, get_info 16, obj_get 16, raw_tracepoint 12, btf_load 28"
    ]
  },
